==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|maihem||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|mayme}}, {{m|enm|mahaime}}, from {{der|en|xno|mahaim||mutilation}}, from {{der|en|fro|mahaign||bodily harm, loss of limb}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*maidijaną||to cripple, injure}} (compare {{cog|gmh|[[meidem]], [[meiden]]||[[gelding]]}}, {{cog|non|meiða||to injure}}, {{cog|got|𐌼𐌰𐌹𐌳𐌾𐌰𐌽||to alter, falsify}}),<ref>Philip Babcock, ed., ''Webster’s Third New International Dictionary of the English Language'', Unabridged, s.v. "mayhem" (Springfield, Mass: Merriam-Webster, Inc., 1993.</ref> from {{der|en|ine-pro|*mey-||to change}}. More at {{m|en|mad}}. The original meaning referred to the crime of [[maim]]ing, the other senses derived from this.

Another possible etymology derives the Old French from Provençal {{m|oc|maganhar}}, composed of {{m|oc|mal||evil}} and {{m|oc|ganhar||to obtain, receive}} (compare with {{cog|es|ganar}} and {{cog|it|gavagnare}} and {{m|it|guadagnare}}), so literally "to obtain, receive something evil).

The sense "chaos" may have arisen by popular misunderstanding of the common [[journalese]] expression "[[rioting]] and mayhem".

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmeɪhɛm/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-mayhem.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# A [[state]] or situation of great [[confusion]], [[disorder]], [[trouble]] or [[destruction]]; [[chaos]].
#: {{ux|en|What if the legendary hero Robin Hood had been born into the '''mayhem''' of the 20th century?}}
#: {{ux|en|In all the '''mayhem''', some children were separated from their partners.}}
#: {{ux|en|She waded into the '''mayhem''', elbowing between taller men to work her way to the front of the crowd.}}
#: {{ux|en|The clowns would dart into the crowd and pull another unsuspecting victim into the '''mayhem''' of the ring.}}
# Infliction of violent injury on a person or thing.
#: {{ux|en|The fighting dogs created '''mayhem''' in the flower beds.}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} The [[maim]]ing of a person by depriving him of the use of any of his limbs which are necessary for defense or protection.
# {{lb|en|legal}} The [[crime]] of [[damaging]] things or [[harming]] people on purpose.

